   243	[P,Q]=\sum_{\ell\ge0}C_\ell h^\ell,
   244	\]
   245	
   246	where, with out-of-range digits set to zero,
   247	
   248	\[
   249	C_\ell=
   250	\sum_{i+j=\ell}[A_i,B_j]
   251	+\sum_{i+j=\ell+1}
   252	\left(iA_i[h,B_j]-jB_j[h,A_i]\right).
   253	\tag{H}
   254	\]
   255	
   256	For example,
   257	
   258	\[
   259	C_0=[A_0,B_0]+A_1[h,B_0]-B_1[h,A_0].
   260	\]
   261	
   262	These are *raw* coefficients in an independent symbol before (T=h).
   263	Actual (h)-adic comparison needs carries.
   264	
   265	### 3.2 Canonical carry recursion
   266	
   267	Set (K_0=0).  Recursively perform monic Euclidean division in
   268	(k[\gamma][\pi]):
   269	
   270	\[
   271	C_\ell+K_\ell=R_\ell+hK_{\ell+1},qquad
   272	\deg_\pi R_\ell<d.
   273	\tag{C}
   274	\]
   275	
   276	Continue through every terminal carry.  Then
   277	
   278	\[
   279	[P,Q]=\sum_{\ell\ge0}R_\ell h^\ell,
   280	\]
   281	
   282	and the exact level-by-level condition is
   283	
   284	\[
   285	J(P,Q)=c\gamma^k
   286	\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
   287	R_0=c\gamma^k,qquad R_\ell=0\ (\ell\ge1).
   288	\tag{L}
   289	\]
   290	
   291	It is generally invalid to impose (C_0=c\gamma^k) and (C_\ell=0)
   292	coefficientwise: products and brackets of digits can have
   293	(\pi)-degree at least (d) and feed higher levels via (C).  Formally, the
   294	Jacobian condition says that the independent-(T) expression differs from
   295	(c\gamma^k) by a multiple of (T-h); it does not say its (T)-coefficients
   296	vanish.
   297	
   298	Even in an added no-carry model, the top-down equations usually control one
   299	combination per rung.  Writing (a_r=A_{p-r}), (b_r=B_{q-r}), with
   300	(a_0=b_0=1), the raw level (p+q-r-1) has the form
   301	
   302	\[
   303	C_{p+q-r-1}=
   304	\sum_{a+b=r+1}[a_a,b_b]
   305	+\sum_{a+b=r}
   306	\bigl((p-a)a_a\delta b_b-(q-b)b_b\delta a_a\bigr).
   307	\]
   308	
   309	If (a_1=0) and (b_1\in k), it reduces to
   310	(\delta(pb_r-qa_r)+\Psi_r), with (\Psi_r) involving earlier levels.
   311	It does not separately make (a_r) and (b_r) constant.  A further
   312	centralizer hypothesis such as
   313	(\ker[h,-]=k[h]) would turn a lower-(\pi)-degree element in the kernel
   314	into a constant, but that hypothesis is neither automatic nor sufficient to
   315	separate the two digits.
   316	
   317	### 3.3 Correction of the charged ((2,3)) display
   318	
   319	For
   320	
   321	\[
   322	f=h^2+2\beta,qquad g=h^3+G_1h+G_0,
   323	\]
   324	
   325	direct Leibniz expansion gives
   326	
   327	\[
   328	\boxed{
   329	\begin{aligned}
   330	J(f,g)={}&h^2\bigl(2J(h,G_1)+6J(\beta,h)\bigr)\\
   331	&+h\bigl(2J(h,G_0)+2J(\beta,G_1)\bigr)\\
   332	&+2G_1J(\beta,h)+2J(\beta,G_0).
   333	\end{aligned}}
   334	\tag{2,3}
   335	\]
   336	
   337	The charged formula shifts (6J(\beta,h)) from the (h^2)-coefficient to
   338	the (h)-coefficient and omits (2J(\beta,G_1)).  Actual minus charged is
   339	
   340	\[
   341	6(h^2-h)J(\beta,h)+2hJ(\beta,G_1).
   342	\]
   343	
   344	The exact control
   345	
   346	\[
   347	h=\pi,quad\beta=\gamma/2,quad G_1=3\gamma/2,quad G_0=0
   348	\]
   349	
   350	has (J(f,g)=3\gamma/2), whereas the charged right side is
   351	(-3\pi^2+3\pi+3\gamma/2).
   352	
   353	In Moh's specialization (G_1=3\beta, G_0=3\alpha/2), the (h^2)-terms
   354	cancel.  If (\beta^2=\alpha h+\Gamma), (2,3) simplifies further to
   355	
   356	\[
   357	J(f,g)=3\bigl(J(\beta,\alpha)-J(h,\Gamma)\bigr).
   358	\]
   359	
   360	Even this expression must be interpreted through exact polynomial identities,
   361	not by treating unreduced powers of (h) as independent.
