   856	## 10. Final typed answer
   857	
   858	The (\eta)-adic first rung is real and exact, but it is the only proved
   859	degree-independent rung.  The general (h)-adic equations are the coupled
   860	bracket-and-carry system (H)--(L); they do not force individual digits to be
   861	constant without additional centralizer, no-carry, and separation input.
   862	
   863	On Moh's shapes, the nonconstant digit degrees happen to satisfy the proposed
   864	bound before the final Jacobian solve, but both normalized (C\ne0) loci are
   865	empty.  The ((16,12)) scalar count (17\to10) is reproduced; the requested
   866	((15,10)) count 22 is from an earlier ansatz than the supplied 12-parameter
   867	shape and is therefore not reconstructible from it.
   868	
   869	Globally, the family in §5 has fixed (k,p,q=1,r), arbitrarily large
   870	(d=re), and one canonical nonconstant digit of
   871	(\gamma)-degree (d/r), containing (\Theta(d)) nonconstant inner
   872	coefficients.  Hence no uniform obstruction, and no finite computation
   873	independent of (d), follows from T-LADDER as stated.  The restriction
   874	(q\ge2), together with a separate (\pi)-profile theorem and genuine
   875	control of the coefficients of (h), remains `OPEN`.

