+# T-LADDER — monomial Jacobians and approximate-root digits
+
+Lane: `t-ladder-sol56-20260903`  
+Date: 2026-09-03  
+Status: **PROVED-HERE / UNREVIEWED**, with every source claim separately marked `SOURCE-READ`  
+Writes: this report and `box/tladder-drivers-20260903/` only; no ledger edits; no `jc2-lean`
+
+## 0. Verdict
+
+The proposed T-LADDER is **false as stated**, but the counterexample lies on the
+reduced-degree boundary \(q=1\).  The intended descended strata
+\((p,q)=(3,2)\) and \((4,3)\) remain **OPEN**.  More precisely:
+
+1. **PROVED-HERE.**  For every fixed \(k\geq0\), fixed \(p,r\geq2\), and
+   arbitrarily large \(e>k+1\), there are monic pairs
+   \((P,Q)\in k[\gamma,\pi]^2\) with
+   
+   \[
+   J_{\gamma,\pi}(P,Q)=\gamma^k,\qquad
+   (\deg P,\deg Q)=(\deg_\pi P,\deg_\pi Q)=(pre,re),
+   \]
+   
+   whose canonical \(H\)-adic expansion is
+   \(P=H^p+U,\ Q=H\), but
+   \(\deg_\gamma U=e>k+1\).  At \(k=0\) these are polynomial automorphisms.
+   Thus the asserted degree bound fails even with fixed reduced pair
+   \((p,q)=(p,1)\).  The sole exceptional digit contains
+   \(\Theta(e)=\Theta(d)\) nonconstant inner \(\pi\)-coefficients and \(e\)
+   free scalar parameters, where \(d=re\).
+
+2. **PROVED-HERE.**  If “number of coefficients” means outer \(H\)-digit
+   indices, it is already at most \(p+q\) before using the Jacobian equation.
+   That reading is tautological and cannot reproduce Moh's counts
+   \(22[15\text{ or }13]\) or \(17\to10\), which count scalar parameters
+   *inside* \(h\) and its digits.  If it means the inner \(\pi\)-coefficient
+   functions, the counterfamily has \(\Theta(d)\) nonconstant ones.
+
+3. **SOURCE-READ + PROVED-HERE.**  The \((16,12)\) control genuinely gives
+   \(17\to10\).  In the normalized ten-parameter family there are five
+   nonconstant canonical \(h\)-digits, all of \(x\)-degree at most \(1\)
+   (hence at most \(k+1=2\)).  The exact system
+   \(J(f,g)=Cx,\ C\ne0\), however, is empty.  It therefore supplies no
+   nonvacuous theorem saying that an existing monomial-Jacobian pair has
+   constant digits.
+
+4. **SOURCE-READ + PROVED-HERE.**  The requested \((15,10)\) positive control
+   mixes two stages.  Moh states \(22[15\text{ or }13]\) on p.208, then states
+   \(12[10\text{ or }7]\) after the further \(\eta\)-simplification on p.209.
+   Pp.210--211 begin after that simplification and display exactly twelve
+   parameters \(a_1,\ldots,a_{12}\), not 22.  The frozen shape can reproduce
+   12, three nonconstant \(h\)-digits, and their maximum \(x\)-degree
+   \(2\leq k+1=3\); it cannot honestly reconstruct the omitted
+   22-parameter ansatz.  Its exact \(J(f,g)=Cx^2,\ C\ne0\) locus is empty.
+
+5. **PROVED-HERE.**  The \(h\)-adic identity quoted in the charge and in
+   frozen m2-descent §4.3 is algebraically wrong: it moves one term down an
+   \(h\)-level and omits another.  The corrected identity and the required
+   Euclidean carry rule are given in §3.
+
+6. **SOURCE-READ / correction to the charged reading.**  Moh's pp.173--174
+   explicitly require denominator shedding when a raw terminal exponent is
+   \(M_h=n-1\).  Such an exponent is dropped from the effective
+   characteristic pairs before Definition 5.1(3) is used.  Consequently the
+   zero denominator called `OPEN[DESCENT-ANCHOR]` in the charged Opus report
+   is an indexing error, not a source-defined obstruction.  The affected
+   rows must be recomputed after shedding; they must not be declared
+   undefined.
+
+The only unconditional degree-independent rigidity established here is the
+exact monomial-\(\eta\) lemma in §2.  No source theorem transports it to
+canonical \(h\)-adic digits.
+
+## 1. Gate, source scope, and conventions
+
+### 1.1 Frozen-input gate
+
+All eight hashes were checked before any source was read or any file was
+written.  They matched exactly:
+
+```text
+2e4e817267cbfdba97607a41df0433b11f3d4542dbb5418226aa48982830accd  ideation-20260903T1200Z-opus5.md
