+\(h^2\)); the remainder rings and degree bounds are asserted.  The two empty
+certificates do not call a black-box `sat()` wrapper: they work on the
+\(C\ne0\) localization by explicit branching and polynomial gcds.  The
+literal \((16,12)\) family is explicitly marked unsolved rather than being
+identified with its normalized editorial/gauge reading.
